[
 "In 1940,", "a brand-new bridge", "in Washington State", "started to dance.",
 "Locals called it", "Galloping Gertie,", "and people drove across", "just to feel it bounce.",
 "Its main span", "was over half", "a mile long,", "but its deck", "was only eight feet deep.",
 "In the wind,", "it rippled like a ribbon.",
 "On November seventh,", "four months", "after it opened,", "a steady wind", "of about forty", "miles an hour", "began to blow.",
 "Then the motion changed.", "The bounce", "turned into a twist.",
 "As the deck tilted,", "the wind caught it", "at an angle", "and pushed it further.",
 "Every twist", "fed the next one.", "The wind was pumping", "energy in faster", "than the bridge", "could lose it.",
 "This is real film", "from that morning.",
 "One man fled his car", "on the bridge,", "with his daughter's dog,", "Tubby,", "still inside.",
 "Around eleven,", "the deck tore loose", "and fell into the water.",
 "For decades,", "textbooks blamed resonance,", "the wind matching", "the bridge's rhythm.",
 "It wasn't.", "The bridge made", "its own rhythm,", "and the wind", "kept feeding it.",
 "That's why big bridges", "are now tested", "in wind tunnels", "before they're built.",
 "So they never", "learn to dance."
]
